  "id": "COMPOUND:27653 - PROTEIN:5854",
  "verbalization": "Prejadomycin is implicated in the biological pathway leading to LNCaP through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Prejadomycin targets Hepatocyte, which in turn is a target of various compounds, including 2-Hexenyl-beta-glucopyranoside and Diosmetin 7-O-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-[Alpha-L-Rhamnopyranosyl-(1->6)]-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside, both of which ultimately target LNCaP. This indicates a potential indirect relationship where Prejadomycin influences LNCaP via these intermediate targets. The evidence is consistent across different paths, suggesting a possible mechanism involving cellular targets that are downstream in the pathway. The integration of these findings supports the notion that Prejadomycin may exert its effects on LNCaP through a complex network of molecular interactions, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
